# The federation profile (PF_PROFILE=federation ./up.sh): PingFederate as its own Trust Anchor, for the
# conformance suite's OpenID Federation plans. up.sh appends it to vars.env and substitutes the issuer
# on its OIDF_FEDERATION_* lines, as it does on vars.env's own.
#
# vars.env already names PF as its own anchor and controller (OIDF_FEDERATION_TRUST_ANCHORS,
# OIDF_FEDERATION_TRUST_CONTROLLER_HOST), so its entity configuration says it is a Trust Anchor and
# publishes fetch, list and resolve. What vars.env leaves out, on purpose, is any key to check a chain
# with - the FAPI, SSF and CIBA plans want federation inert. This adds PF's own keys, read from its
# signing key store whenever a chain is checked, so nothing is pinned before PF has booted and a key
# rotation needs no change: the resolve endpoint answers for PF, and the registration filters validate
# chains that end at it.
OIDF_FEDERATION_SELF_ANCHOR=https://localhost:9031
OIDF_FEDERATION_ORGANIZATION_NAME=pf-agentic-identity conformance rig
